  "description": "WADRAY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H90 Ce6 N4 O34 2+,2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.608-4.007 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.90-115.82°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C104H90Ce6N6O40. Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV), Ce(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
